============================================================
IMPORTANT DIFFERENCES TO REMEMBER
============================================================

1. WHERE vs HAVING

WHERE → filters rows
HAVING → filters groups


2. COUNT(*) vs COUNT(column)

COUNT(*) → counts all rows
COUNT(column) → counts non-NULL values


3. % vs _

% → any number of characters
_ → exactly one character


4. DISTINCT vs normal SELECT

DISTINCT → unique values only
Normal SELECT → duplicates may appear


5. ASC vs DESC

ASC → smallest/A-Z first
DESC → largest/Z-A first


6. BETWEEN

BETWEEN is inclusive.

BETWEEN 2500 AND 5000

includes:

2500
5000


7. COALESCE

COALESCE(column, 0)

→ returns column value if available
→ returns 0 if column is NULL


